      "id": 1,
      "text": "Silver Creek’s roots trace back to post‑Civil‑War settlement, where the 1869 Methodist Church and 1875 Presbyterian Church became community anchors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/silver_creek_georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits near the confluence of the Etowah and Oostanaula Rivers, whose merge north of Rome forms the Coosa River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
